  "slug": "arabidopsis-mediated-f99c",
  "summary": "New papers resolve hormone control to specific promoters, DNA methylation, histone marks and splice events across ABA, JA, cytokinin and auxin pathways.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is regulation of hormone metabolism and sensitivity at defined genomic or transcript targets, with ABA the most frequent node. GhNAC029 represses GhNCED1 in cotton, and RhWUS1 represses RhNCED3 in rose, where cytokinin and auxin factors also act on it. In Brassica, promoter methylation of BraCYP707A3.A02 blocks BraBPC2.A08 binding, linking ABA catabolism to clubroot resistance. In Arabidopsis, SRPKII kinases shape ABA sensitivity via SR45 and HAB1 splicing, and ANAC030 promotes senescence through JA synthesis. Chromatin-level items add context: RSI1/FLD demethylates H3K4me2/3 at its own TSS to limit pathogen-induced expression, and maize H2A.Z mapping links the histone variant to tissue-specific expression. New is the resolution to specific promoters, epigenetic marks and splice events.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
